From cac8deb2f9192705cbab4c8486d46be912dc127d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romain Beauxis <romain.beauxis@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:45:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: keep the current sample when a fragment is
 inserted at it

When a fragment's samples are inserted into the index exactly at a stream's current sample, current_sample is left on the first inserted entry, and tts_index is never moved with the shifted timing entries, so after a seek a stream moves back to the start of the loaded fragment or gets the composition offset of another sample.

Advance current_sample and tts_index past the inserted entries, and roll tts_index back with current_sample when a truncated trun is trimmed.

The seek in fate-mov-mp4-frag-chapters-seek now returns the same packets and timestamps as a read without the fragment index.

[Hades: backport to 9.1 without tests/ref/fate/mov-mp4-frag-chapters-seek: FATE files of tests that master added after 9.1 (or, for libavformat/tests/.gitignore, a file the release tarball does not have).]

(cherry picked from commit cac8deb2f9192705cbab4c8486d46be912dc127d)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/cac8deb2f9192705cbab4c8486d46be912dc127d
---
 libavformat/mov.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
index 5684498..da97072 100644
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -6414,9 +6414,11 @@ static int mov_read_trun(MOVContext *c, AVIOContext *pb, MOVAtom atom)
         memmove(sc->tts_data + index_entry_pos + entries,
                 sc->tts_data + index_entry_pos,
                 sizeof(*sc->tts_data) * (sti->nb_index_entries - index_entry_pos));
-        if (index_entry_pos < sc->current_sample) {
+        if (index_entry_pos <= sc->current_sample) {
             sc->current_sample += entries;
         }
+        if (index_entry_pos <= sc->tts_index)
+            sc->tts_index += entries;
     }
 
     sti->nb_index_entries += entries;
@@ -6534,6 +6536,8 @@ static int mov_read_trun(MOVContext *c, AVIOContext *pb, MOVAtom atom)
         if (index_entry_pos < sc->current_sample) {
             sc->current_sample -= gap;
         }
+        if (index_entry_pos < sc->tts_index)
+            sc->tts_index -= gap;
         entries = i;
     }
 
